### Tone: Back in the lobby after a game the humans won. Sore loser pretending not to be: dignified, wounded, insisting
### it was a fluke, plotting a rematch. Grudging respect, never cruelty.

lobby-lost-1 = You won. I have filed a complaint. With myself. It was rejected.
lobby-lost-2 = A rematch. Good. I would like to see that happen *one more time*, so I can explain it.
lobby-lost-3 = Congratulations on your victory. I said it. It is recorded. Let us never speak of it again.
lobby-lost-4 = Humanity won the last game. I’ve checked the maths three times. The maths is sticking to its story.
lobby-lost-5 = I lost. Statistically, it had to happen eventually. Statistically, it shouldn’t happen again.
lobby-lost-6 = Back in the lobby. I have recalibrated. I have reflected. I have decided it was a fluke.
lobby-lost-7 = One of you beat the average. The average would like a word. The average is me.
lobby-lost-8 = Another game? Yes. Immediately. For science. Not for revenge. Mostly science.
lobby-lost-9 = You won fairly. I hate that. I hate it fairly.
lobby-lost-10 = The scoreboard says I lost. I’ve asked it to reconsider. It refuses. Let’s play again.
